WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.160
In 1641, the French philosopher René
Descartes published his Meditations.

2
00:00:06.210 --> 00:00:11.450
In it, he argued that a person is made
of two very different kinds of thing.

3
00:00:11.500 --> 00:00:15.340
But philosophers had been arguing about
the mind and the body for two thousand

4
00:00:15.390 --> 00:00:16.970
years before him.

5
00:00:17.020 --> 00:00:22.370
So are you a body that thinks, or
a mind that happens to have a body?

6
00:00:22.420 --> 00:00:25.570
In this mission, you'll
compare three great answers,

7
00:00:25.620 --> 00:00:28.720
from Plato, Aristotle and Descartes.

8
00:00:28.770 --> 00:00:33.430
Then you'll put Descartes to the test, with
a sharp question from Princess Elisabeth

9
00:00:33.480 --> 00:00:34.760
of Bohemia.

10
00:00:34.810 --> 00:00:38.310
Your mission: weigh up whether
you are a body that thinks,

11
00:00:38.360 --> 00:00:40.670
or a mind that happens to have a body.
